# The container-fleet spec (the wire-acceptance fleet; baked, not IMDS —
# the IMDS user-data fetch is broken on the real wire (the per-attempt LLA
# re-add fails with EOPNOTSUPP -95), so the fleet spec is baked into the
# bundle rootfs at /etc/wardend/fleet. The spec parser (spec::parse_lines)
# reads this file directly (load_fleet_spec) — NOT the broken IMDS path.
#
# The container line (the backend) must precede the host line (a dangling
# backend is a hard error in the spec parser).
# The udunit vhost was REMOVED from the default boot (de-host campaign
# ruling: a second outside host whose backend is spawned by nothing — a
# dead-backend route; masked pre-deletion by the legacy page, post-
# deletion a 404. Single-outside-host doctrine). The container+host pair
# moved together (a dangling backend is a spec-parser hard error).
#
# The capstone's second vhost (the stock-nginx concept-proof): the
# `container` line declares the backend name (the spec parser's hard-error
# check: a dangling backend is a typo); the `host` line binds the domain
# to the backend (the SNI -> backend UDS route: /run/wardend/nginx.sock,
# spawned by the seed's `unit` directive). The second domain gets a cert
# as well (a second ACME order, the same seald HSM key); both domains
# are served over HTTPS with real certs (the SNI routes the domain to the
# backend UDS).
# COMMENTED-OUT (de-host campaign ruling: nginx = comment-out encoding,
# single-outside-host doctrine — nginx-srv rides as opt-in proof config).
# The WHOLE nginx-referencing cluster moves together (parser-relevant is
# FOUR lines, not the unit-of-three phrase): container(19) + both hosts
# (20 + acme-test 25) — commenting the container while acme-test's
# backend=nginx stays live is a dangling-backend HARD ERROR at boot.
# acme-test rides with its only backend (its domain was an nginx
# concept-proof; a live backend-less host line is the hard-error class).
#container docker.io/library/nginx:latest name=nginx
#host nginx.lrvick.dev backend=nginx
#host acme-test.cautionos.dev backend=nginx
# The capstone's ACME domain (real LE-issued cert, our own TLS 1.3 ACME
# client + seald HSM key). Rode the nginx backend (the SNI route) — now
# riding the comment-out with the cluster.
#
# KEEP-ACTIVE (chipmunk ruling + squid source check, auditable):
# the acme= line stays LIVE with zero host lines. Verified host-line-
# driven, NOT cert-store-driven: acme_thread iterates state.domains
# (wire.rs:3223; populated ONLY from spec host lines at :2941/:3560),
# gated on state.active (PointsToSelf DNS poll, :3221-3224); zero host
# lines = zero iterations = zero orders = the line is INERT. No cert-
# store enumeration exists: cert_dir is WRITE-ONLY (write_cert :3293-
# 3302 is the only disk touch; s.certs written only at :3250, in-memory)
# and /run/wardend/certs is TMPFS — capstone-era certs cannot persist
# across boots and drive nothing. Inert-but-warm beats inert-and-cold:
# commenting buys zero safety and hides a cutover dependency (§9 row 7:
# deploy is ACME-issuance-dependent for the System Health host-add).
#
# The baked STAGING argv fallback (chipmunk hcl cite, verified at pin
# 72ae8b0 bastiond.hcl:65 = command [--acme-url
# https://acme-staging-v02.api.letsencrypt.org/directory]): with NO fleet
# acme= line, a setdomain'd host falls to the baked STAGING URL -> the
# browser verifier pins the PRODUCTION ISRG root -> fail CLOSED. So this
# production acme= line is LOAD-BEARING for the cutover (it is the ONLY
# thing that makes a host-add issue a production-rooted cert), not mere
# bookkeeping. Keep it live.
acme=https://acme-v02.api.letsencrypt.org/directory
#
# System Health (the de-host campaign destination, D1): posternd's new
# HTTP face on the dedicated http.sock UDS, reached by the bastiond SNI
# route table. grammar locked: backend name == the socket stem on the
# DEVICES PLANE (backend_uds() -> "/run/wardend/devices/{name}.sock" at
# the bastiond route builder; the container line declares the name so the
# parser's dangling-backend check is satisfied — posternd is spawned by
# its OWN unit, the image ref here is inert declaration grammar, exactly
# like the retired nginx block).
# The backend=http resolves to /run/wardend/devices/http.sock
# (DEFAULT_HTTP_SOCK, http.rs:61). The devices/ dir is the SHARED
# CROSS-NS RENDEZVOUS PLANE (the per-daemon-sandbox split makes bare
# /run/wardend namespace-private; every cross-sandbox face rides devices/
# — :22's postern.sock was its first consumer). Domain = the operator's
# stated end-state (verify.cautionos
# .dev); the only prod-time change on this line is DNS + ACME issuance
# (PointsToSelf gates on real-IP answers — an operator deploy concern).
container docker.io/library/posternd:latest name=http
host verify.cautionos.dev backend=http
